<title>NEW ZEALAND: NZ revises 1996/97 budget surplus down.</title>
<headline>NZ revises 1996/97 budget surplus down.</headline>
<dateline>WELLINGTON 1997-05-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>The New Zealand Treasury in its Current-year Fiscal Update (CFU) on Wednesday revised its forecast for the 1996/97 budget to NZ$2.312 billion from NZ$2.493 billion in the previous forecast in the December Econonomic and Fiscal Update (DEFU).</p>
<p>The following is a table of forecasts compared with previous forecasts:  </p>
<p>The following is a table of forecasts compared with previous forecasts:</p>
<p>			    CFU		 DEFU	    BUDGET</p>
<p>Revenue (bln)	   35.2		35.5	    35.4</p>
<p>Expenses (bln)	  33.2		33.2	    32.9</p>
<p>Surplus (bln)	    2.3		 2.5	     2.8</p>
<p>Surplus/GDP (pct)	2.4		 2.6	     2.9</p>
<p>Net worth (bln)	  5.9		 6.0	     6.0</p>
<p>Net debt (bln)	  25.5		26.1	    27.4</p>
<p>Net debt/GDP (pct)    26.7		27.3	    29.0</p>
<p>-- Wellington newsroom 64 4 4734 746</p>
